   "source": [
    "Our original VIF showed high values with mmr, make, and body. Mmr is a market estimate for the worth of the vehicle so it made sense that predictor overpowered all of the other predictors. Likewise, it's a pretty safe assumption that the vehicle model was already capturing the make and body. For example a vehicle model of 'Ram 1500' only refers to a dodge truck so the model can easily deduce that data from the vehicle model so including those in the model was redundant.\n",
    "\n",
    "Our current model shows no VIF values above or close to 10 so there appear to be no concerns there."
